  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sindh Education Non-State Actors (SENSA) Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sindh Education Non-State Actors programme (SENSA) will fund a full cycle of primary education for 53,614 (59% girls, 41% boys) of the poorest children in Sindh.This will make a dramatic difference to the lives of 53,614 of the most marginalised, poorest and disadvantaged children in Sindh. SENSA will help educate 2.1% of the total number of out-of-school girls in Sindh and provide hope and opportunity for their families and communities</narrative>
  </description>
